//? Title: Truncated backoff: windows, slots and retry limits
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Repeated colliding transmissions need different retry delays. Binary exponential
backoff widens the candidate slot window, caps its exponent, then abandons a
frame after a fixed collision count.
)

\toc

> The method

For c≥0, W(c)=2^min(c,10). A caller fraction u∈[0,1) maps to slot floor(uW), so
every slot occupies an interval of length1/W. The ideal mean is (W−1)/2 and two
independent ideal uniform stations collide again with probability1/W. These are
probability calculations, not network throughput measurements. At c≥16 the
policy abandons the frame even though its descriptive window is still1024.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/truncated_backoff_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/truncated_binary_exponential_backoff.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    int w = a::contention_window(3), slot = a::backoff_slot(3, .5);
    std::print("| collisions | window | caller u | actual slot | abandon " "|\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n|3|{}|.5|{}|{}|\n",
               w, slot, a::backoff_give_up(3));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "3 collisions; supplied u=.5");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual window {}", w));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual slot {}", slot));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/truncated_backoff_tiny.svg");
}
```
